  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The three quantum numbers $n, l$ and $m$ that describe an orbital has integer values of 0,1,2,3 and so on.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_che_a53.png\">\r\nThe electronic arrangement of option (c) is absurd because\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nn=2 \\\\\r\nl=0 \\\\\r\nm=0\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nTo sum up, where $n=2, l=0, m=0$ Hence, for $l=0,$ value of $m$ should be zero.",
    "image": null
  },
